From a0ac52fb2956730e6821c7fbc1620ace890e286f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WeiguangTWK <weiguangtwk@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:52:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Neko LineageOS: [ASTER] integrate offline KernelSU
 verification and resident evidence

Extend KernelSU source requests with an offline manager-APK channel.
Resolve the installed manager APK as an input locator and leave source
authentication and module extraction to the ASTER executor.

Distinguish complete loading-input evidence from partial resident
evidence. Bind requests and reports to the appropriate load_id or
resident_id and reject mixed instance identifiers.

Integrate verified KernelSU evidence into effective classification and
the existing mode-specific policy. Allow verified KSU findings to be
reconciled with compromise-mode history while retaining unrelated
alarms and verification failures.

Parse explicit resident sampling progress and present CHECKING while
supported comparisons are pending. Preserve higher-priority findings,
evidence-loss handling and existing permit conditions.

Change-Id: I12b220a0ae5049c9e575f6b408c86e57053f5ae1
